<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct gold imports plunge 65.8 pct yr/yr - MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct gold imports plunge 65.8 pct yr/yr - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gold imports in October plunged 65.8 percent from a year earlier to 6.91 tonnes, Finance Ministry data released on Thursday showed.  </p>
<p>The figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			   Oct 96    Sept 96    Oct 95</p>
<p> Total		   6.91	7.86	 20.20</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Australia	     0.85	1.82	  4.81</p>
<p> South Africa	  1.58	0.52	  3.14</p>
<p> Britain		 1.00	1.63	  1.50</p>
<p> Canada		  0.50	0.50	  2.35</p>
<p> South Korea	   0.30	0.70	  0.60</p>
<p> Switzerland	   0.59	0.01	  4.57</p>
<p>Gold imports in the first 10 months of 1996 totalled 119.88 tonnes, against 234.96 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 7431)</p>
</text>
